package Libraries.Web.Styles

/*
    WebStyle is the parent of every kind of style for a web page. A style
    says how an element looks: its text, its list markers, its spacing. It
    never says where the items inside go; that is a layout's job, so a
    style and a layout never set the same thing. A style is set on an
    element through the page, with SetStyle, and only a kind of style that
    fits that element is accepted. The website's build turns each style
    into a stylesheet rule, so a style never needs any CSS from the person
    using it.

    WebStyle itself can't be used on its own. Use one of its children,
    such as WebListStyle or WebTextStyle.

    Attribute: Example
    use Libraries.Web.Page.all
    use Libraries.Web.Styles.WebListStyle

    class Main is WebPage
        action Main
            WebListStyle bullets
            bullets:UseDiscs()
            bullets:SetLeftPadding(32)

            UnorderedList list
            SetStyle(list, bullets)
            list:AddListItem("First")
            list:AddListItem("Second")
            Add(list)
        end
    end
*/
class WebStyle
    /*
        Returns the stylesheet declarations for this style: the settings
        inside one rule, without the rule's name. Every kind of style
        writes its own. WebSite calls this when it writes the stylesheet;
        people making pages don't.

        Attribute: Returns The declarations for this style, or nothing if it needs none.
    */
    blueprint action Generate returns text
end
